  "findings": [
    "The same staged policy and seed survives to 180s under stochastic action selection in two one-episode probes.",
    "The traced stochastic run reaches the 60s handoff near the bottom edge but not pinned to the left corner; health is 113.2499 instead of the deterministic trace's 92.4698.",
    "From 60s to 75s, stochastic sampling includes actions 0, 3, 4, 6, 7, and 8 instead of deterministic action 7 only, which lets the player move away from the corner before pressure attaches.",
    "By 89.999s the player has recovered to x = -222.8753 with boundary_min_distance 57.6392 and no low-health risk, while the deterministic run had already dropped to 24.8195 health.",
    "This does not make stochastic evaluation an acceptance gate, but it shows that the policy distribution contains recovery actions that deterministic argmax suppresses."
  ],
